<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Barcelona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/878">878</a>–<a href="/years/1410">1410</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> was the dynasty of counts of Barcelona descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy">Wilfred the Hairy</a>, who gathered several Catalan counties under one line in the late 9th century. By the marriage of Ramon Berenguer IV and Petronilla in 1137 it acquired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a> and ruled the Crown of Aragon until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-of-aragon">Martin the Humane</a> died in 1410.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Its counts were often in conflict with the counts of Barcelona and the bishops of Girona, while remaining vassals of the <b>House of Barcelona</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-empuries">County of Empúries</a></li><li><blockquote>Osona remained in the hands of the <b>House of Barcelona</b>, briefly granted to younger sons, until it was fully merged with the County of Barcelona.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-osona">County of Osona</a></li><li><blockquote>They became vassals of the <b>Counts of Barcelona</b> and later the Crown of Aragon, but kept wide local powers.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-pallars-sobira">County of Pallars Sobirà</a></li><li><blockquote>Later the county passed to a branch of the royal <b>House of Barcelona</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-urgell">County of Urgell</a></li><li><blockquote>Its rulers, all freedmen, lacked dynastic legitimacy and leaned on stronger neighbours such as Dénia and Zaragoza, and on payments to the <b>Counts of Barcelona</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/taifa-of-tortosa">Taifa of Tortosa</a></li></ul></section>
